+# Pi and OpenCode: removing locally acting tools
+
+Task: **TASK-261010-aqpf2a — research-pi-opencode-tool-disable**. Research snapshot: **2026-10-10 task date**. Status: **ready for review**.
+
+This is source and documentation research. Neither harness was installed or executed; no harness or repository test suite, login, credential probe, or Keychain access was performed. All recipes below are **proposals for hosted-runner measurement**, not commands run on the research host. “Candidate” means a concrete source-supported configuration to measure; it does not mean a supported or empirically qualified tuple.
+
+The supplied owner rule requires **no locally acting tool offered to the model**. Removing a tool, denying its execution, and confining the process are different properties. CIP-0008 additionally excludes provider-hosted tools outside the relay and permits bounded harness state; CIP-0009 supplies the OS boundary. Both layers are needed. The older Muse exception in the draft does not relax this task's owner rule. [C8] [C9]
